// §14 entry 19 -- mixed-script identifier, single module -> EXS-E0104.
//
// §8.2: "UTS #39 Moderately Restrictive. Mixed-script is EXS-E0104." The
// identifier below mixes Latin 'x' with CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER A (U+0430) --
// one of UTS #39's three named Level-4 exclusions (Latin+Cyrillic,
// Latin+Greek, Latin+Cherokee), which tests/unit/lexer_ident_scripts.asm
// also exercises directly.
//
// Different in kind from entry 4: this is ONE identifier in ONE module
// (mixed script within a single name), not two confusable identifiers
// across an import closure -- §8.2 draws that line explicitly, and this
// entry sits on the side a single-file lexer CAN already decide.
//
// RUNS this wave: lexer/lex.inc's `lex_script_ok` already implements this
// exactly (verified by actually running this fixture through
// tests/conformance/tools/lex_probe -- see run_conformance_tests).

publica functio saluta() -> textus {
    firma xа = "Ave, mundus."
    redde xа
}

